@@3
From: Susan Oyelaran
To: Marcus Feld
Subj: Re: Hello, world, the ARM way
Date: 07-13-88 22:05

> So how do you print a dollar sign???

With a different function (02h prints one character from DL, which is
the low byte of r3), or with printf like a civilised person.

> Also how do you tell if the DOS call worked?

Same as on a PC: the carry flag.  The ARM has a real carry flag in the
CPSR, and DOS sets it on an error, so right after the svc:

      svc   #0x21
      bcs   failed          @ carry set: r0 holds the error code

That's the whole trick.  The ARM version is actually tidier, because
every instruction can test the flags, not just the jumps.

Susan
