From: Susan Oyelaran
To: Doc Mantissa
Subj: Re: CLZ: log2 in one instruction
Date: 03-10-89 07:20

> My Mandelbrot got four times faster.

Then here's one more for the collection: moving memory 32 bytes at a
time.  LDM loads eight registers from consecutive addresses in one
instruction, STM stores them, and the "!" moves the pointer along:

  static void copy32(void *dst, const void *src, unsigned blocks)
  {
      __asm__ volatile (
          "1: ldmia %1!, {r3-r10}\n\t"
          "   stmia %0!, {r3-r10}\n\t"
          "   subs  %2, %2, #1\n\t"
          "   bne   1b"
          : "+r" (dst), "+r" (src), "+r" (blocks)
          : : "r3", "r4", "r5", "r6", "r7", "r8", "r9", "r10",
              "cc", "memory");
  }

blocks is the count of 32-byte blocks, at least 1; both pointers
should be word aligned.  Copying a 256-byte table is copy32(b, a, 8).

Susan
