@@13
From: Europa Sysop
To: Marcus Feld
Subj: Re: How do I get the date?
Date: 06-05-89 23:10

> How do I get today's date

INT 21h function 2Ah.  It returns the year in CX, the month in DH and
the day in DL.  On the ARM: CX is r2, DX is r3, so the month is the
second byte of r3 and the day the first:

  static void getdate(int *y, int *m, int *d)
  {
      unsigned cx, dx;
      __asm__ volatile (
          "mov r0, #0x2A00\n\t"         /* AH = 2Ah */
          "svc #0x21\n\t"
          "mov %0, r2\n\t"
          "mov %1, r3"
          : "=r" (cx), "=r" (dx) : : "r0", "r1", "r2", "r3", "cc");
      *y = cx & 0xFFFF;
      *m = (dx >> 8) & 0xFF;
      *d = dx & 0xFF;
  }

(AL comes back with the day of the week, 0 = Sunday, if you want to be
even sadder about Mondays.)  Or in plain C, time() and localtime() work
too; they end up asking DOS the same question.

-- Europa
