From: Bill Tran
To: All
Subj: Timing without the timer chip
Date: 11-19-89 02:20

For anyone writing a door or a game: you don't have to program the
timer to measure time.  The BIOS counts timer ticks, 18.2 of them a
second, in a 32-bit word at address 0x46C (same place as on a PC, only
here it's just an address):

  volatile unsigned long *ticks = (volatile unsigned long *)0x46C;
  unsigned long t0 = *ticks;
  while (*ticks - t0 < 18)       /* about one second */
      ;

The subtraction keeps working when the counter wraps at midnight, as
long as you use unsigned.  My "modem training" animation now runs at the
same speed with TURBO on or off.  My cat is unimpressed.

Bill
