Subj: DOS tips from a Lotus guy
Date: 12-02-89 21:50

I'm not a programmer, but this area has taught me enough DOS to be
dangerous.  Here are the ones I use every day, all tried on my ARM/AT:

  PROMPT $P$G          shows the directory in the prompt: C:\LOTUS>
                       (put it in AUTOEXEC.BAT)
  DIR | SORT           the directory in alphabetical order
  DIR | FIND /C "EXE"  counts the lines with EXE in them
  TREE C:\ /F | MORE   every directory and file, a page at a time
  MEM /PROGRAM         who is using my 640K
  DIR /W               wide listing, five names across
  COPY CON NOTE.TXT    type a file straight in, end with F6 and Enter

The vertical bar is a "pipe".  It hands one program's output to the
next one.  Linda asked what I was doing and I said "piping".  She said
"that's what the plumber said, and then he charged us $300".

Dave
